{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1315637744/14/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b9c3697\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nInsert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.\n- Red components outside structures.\n\nRule:\n- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.\n- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.\n- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.\n- Unmatched reds vanish.\n\nKey insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"60d73be6\" lines=\"22-39\">\n<description>\nComplete the sparse colored marker pattern by reflecting it across a full-row/full-column cross.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and one non-background cross color that\nfills exactly one complete row and one complete column. All other foreground\npixels are sparse markers away from that cross.\n\nRule\nKeep the input unchanged, and for each marker pixel copy its color to the\npositions obtained by reflecting it across the cross row, across the cross\ncolumn, and across both axes. Reflected positions outside the grid are\nclipped.\n\nKey insight\nThe full cross is not a copied object; it is the pair of mirror axes for\ncompleting the quadrant pattern.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22806e14\" lines=\"23-37\">\n<description>\nMark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background.\n- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.\n\nRule:\n- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.\n- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.\n- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e45ef808\" lines=\"31-46\">\n<description>\nMark the shallowest and deepest columns of a solid terrain boundary with vertical colored guide lines.\n\nInput structure:\n- The first row is a solid empty separator.\n- Below it, each column consists of upper fill cells followed by a contiguous suffix of terrain cells.\n- The bottom row is all terrain, so every column has a well-defined first terrain row.\n\nRule:\n- Find the column whose first terrain row is latest; it is unique and its upper fill run becomes maroon.\n- Find the rightmost column whose first terrain row is earliest; its upper fill run becomes yellow.\n- Preserve the empty separator, terrain cells, and all other upper fill cells.\n\nKey insight:\n- The task is a column-height summary of the terrain profile: color the deepest upper run and the highest terrain peak.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2b9ef948\" lines=\"51-65\">\n<description>\nMove the yellow 3x3 frame by the displacement encoded by the gray path, then draw its diagonal yellow corner rays.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is black.\n- One 3x3 yellow frame has a non-yellow control-color center.\n- A second control-color pixel is connected through gray path pixels to a lone yellow endpoint.\n\nRule:\n- Use the vector from the second control-color pixel to the lone yellow endpoint as the frame's translation.\n- Fill the whole output with the control color.\n- Draw the translated yellow frame and extend yellow diagonal rays outward from its four corners to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight: The gray path's turns are irrelevant; its two colored endpoints encode the net displacement to apply to the frame.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\" lines=\"35-46\">\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"37ce87bb\" lines=\"33-47\">\n<description>\nCompute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.\n- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.\n\nRule\n- Keep every input bar unchanged.\n- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.\n- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.\n\nKey insight\n- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"abc82100\" lines=\"70-86\">\n<description>\nUse local source-target-pattern examples to replace matching source pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) pattern components.\n- A rule example is a 4-neighbor colored pair source->target whose continued\n  direction reaches an anchor touching a teal pattern component.\n\nRule:\n- For each rule example, copy that teal component onto every other pixel of\n  source.color, recoloring the copied component to target.color.\n- Translation maps the rule anchor onto the source pixel being replaced.\n- Remove teal components and all pixels used by rule examples.\n\nKey insight: The two adjacent colored pixels define the color substitution and\nthe anchor point; the nearby teal component is the stencil that gets recolored.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"342ae2ed\" lines=\"34-49\">\n<description>\nDraw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\n- Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.\n- The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.\n\nRule:\n- Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.\n- For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.\n- Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.\n\nKey insight:\n- Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"182e5d0f\" lines=\"89-103\">\n<description>\nMove each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n\nRule:\n- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d255d7a7\" lines=\"99-114\">\n<description>\nMove the patterned edge band to the opposite edge along every row or column whose band slice contains the trail color.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- The two foreground colors are a frequent trail color and a rarer marker color.\n- All marker pixels lie nearest to one grid edge, and that edge contains trail-color runs that define the source-band thickness.\n\nRule\n- Choose the source edge identified by the marker pixels.\n- A row or column perpendicular to that edge moves if its source-band slice contains the trail color.\n- Copy that slice unchanged to the opposite edge, erase the remaining trail cells to background, and keep marker-only lines fixed.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color identifies the active edge, while the trail color identifies which parallel rows or columns carry an edge-band slice across the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7ec998c9\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nDraw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
